===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*Hwerdʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|rose}}, {{m|enm|roose}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rōse}}, from {{der|en|la|rosa}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin but possibly via {{der|en|osc|-}} from {{der|en|grc|ῥόδον|t=rose}} (Aeolic {{m|grc|ϝρόδον}}), from {{der|en|peo|sc=Latn|*wṛda-||flower}} (compare {{cog|ae|𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬆𐬜𐬀|𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬆𐬜𐬀-}}, {{cog|sog|ward|sc=Latn}}, {{cog|xpr|wâr|sc=Latn}}, late {{cog|pal|tr=gwl|ts=gul|sc=Latn}}, {{cog|fa|گل|tr=gul|t=rose, flower}}, and Middle Iranian borrowings including {{cog|xcl|վարդ|t=rose}}, {{cog|arc|וַרְדָּא|tr=wardā}} / {{m|syc|ܘܪܕܐ|tr=wardā}}, {{cog|ar|وَرْدَة}}, {{cog|he|וֶרֶד|tr=wéreḏ}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wr̥dʰos||sweetbriar}} (compare {{cog|ang|word||thornbush}}, {{cog|la|rubus||bramble}}, {{cog|sq|hurdhe||ivy}}). Possibly ultimately a derivation from a verb for "to grow" only attested in Indo-Iranian ({{m|iir-pro|*Hwardʰ-}}, compare {{cog|sa|वर्धति}}, with relatives in Avestan).

