====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[shrub]] of the genus ''[[Rosa]]'', with red, pink, white or yellow [[flower]]s.
# A [[flower]] of the rose [[plant]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|II|ii|text=''Iu.'' 'Tis but thy name that is my Enemy:<br>Thou art thy [[self|ſelfe]]...<br>What'[[is|s]] in a [[name]]? That which we call a '''Roſe''',<br>By any other word would [[smell|ſmell]] as [[sweet|ſweete]]...}}
#* '''1794''', {{w|Robert Burns}}, "[[:w:A Red, Red Rose|A Red, Red '''Rose''']]:"
#*: O my [[love|Luve]]'s like a red, red '''rose'''<br>That's newly sprung in [[June|june]]...
#* '''1913''', {{w|Gertrude Stein}}, "Sacred Emily":
#*: [[:w:Rose is a rose is a rose is a rose|Rose is a '''rose''' is a '''rose''' is a '''rose'''.]]
# A plant or species in the rose family. ([[Rosaceae]])
# Something resembling a rose flower.
# {{lb|en|heraldiccharge}} The rose flower, usually depicted with five petals, five barbs, and a circular seed.
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} A [[purple|purplish]]-[[red]] or [[pink]] [[colour]], the colour of some rose flowers.
#: {{color panel|Web rose|FF007F}}
#: {{color panel|[[rose-pink]]|FF66CC}}
# A round [[nozzle]] for a sprinkling can or hose.
# The usually circular base of a light socket in the ceiling, from which the fitting or chandelier is suspended.
# Any of various large, red-bodied, [[papilionid]] butterflies of the [[genus]] {{taxlink|Pachliopta|genus|ver=190708}}.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Any of various flower-like [[polar]] [[graph]]s of [[sinusoid]]s or their [[square]]s. [[Category:en:Curves]]
# {{lb|en|mathematics|graph theory}} A [[graph]] with only one [[vertex]].

